KNOWNBUG
port_conflict1.sv

^\[main\.p0] always main\.a == !main\.a: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Port connections are turned into constraints (build_port_connection in
verilog_rtl.cpp) without going through the multi-driver conflict check
that ordinary continuous assignments use. Two port-connected drivers
that disagree on the same net (i_a.y = a, i_b.y = ~a, both connected to
x) are silently accepted as two contradictory constraints, making the
whole transition system UNSAT. Every property in the module -- even
one entirely unrelated to x, like p0 above -- is then vacuously
reported PROVED (EXIT=0) instead of the correct REFUTED (EXIT=10).
